 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Cursed Circuitry — Innate Technique (1st level)</em></p><blockquote><p>You can apply a circuit that allows for extremely efficient use of cursed energy.</p></blockquote><p>Starting at 1st level, as a bonus action for 2 Cursed Energy, you can apply a <em>Circuit</em> to yourself or an object you touch for 1 minute. You can also apply your <em>Circuit</em> to another willing creature you touch for 5 CE for half the time. Your cursed circuit gives the following:<br />\n<strong>Efficiency</strong>. The base cost of a feature that requires cursed energy other than <em>Cursed Circuitry</em> features decreases by 1 (min cost of 1). If a feature’s effects depend on how much cursed energy you spend, one cursed energy you spend gives the effects of two. (Eg. Spending 2 CE on Cursed Strike counts as 4 CE). This cannot cause the cursed energy to be higher than your output limit.<br />\n<strong>Output</strong>. When a feature allows you to spend additional cursed energy to strengthen the effects, you can spend additional cursed energy up to half to your proficiency bonus (rounded up).<br />\n<strong>Enhancement</strong>. If you apply your circuit onto an Object or Cursed Tool, it instead gains one of the following benefits of your choice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>The item deals an additional 2d4 necrotic damage on a hit.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The item grants a +2 bonus to AC  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The cursed energy cost of the tool decreases by 1 (min of 1)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can only have 1 circuit at a time. This becomes 2 circuits at 3rd level, 3 circuits at 6th, and 4 at 11th level.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
